    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup today is anchored by **Geraldo Perdomo** (67.71) and **Lawrence Butler** (65.73), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Geraldo Perdomo** sits at the top of our daily projections, leveraging a high SP_xERA of 4.65 from Ure\u00f1a and a +16% skill advantage to provide a steady floor. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is our primary source of upside; his 10% park boost and a strong platoon advantage against Jones make him our most potent outfielder. **Bryson Stott** (62.69) also demands attention, not just for his solid base projection, but because he faces Gusto\u2014a pitcher whose delivery speed provides a +4% boost to **Bryson Stott**\u2019s stolen base potential, a critical metric for our roster strategy.\n\nThe decision to start **Tyler Freeman** (58.41) over bench depth like **Brendan Donovan** or **Jung Hoo Lee** was marginal, but ultimately driven by the specific synergy between **Tyler Freeman**\u2019s batting order position and the opposing SP's tendency to allow stolen bases. While **Gleyber Torres** (47.36) remains in the lineup, his score is depressed by a negative platoon split against Teng; he represents our lowest-confidence start today. **Jonathan Aranda** (55.90) and **Masyn Winn** (53.71) occupy the middle tier, with **Masyn Winn** providing a sneaky boost from his high-probability SB environment against Peralta. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Will Smith** all confirmed on the IL, our depth is being tested. We continue to monitor the status of **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert** for potential bench rotation, but for today, the current configuration offers the most efficient path to maximizing our 5x5 categories.",
